if (!sbi->volume_name)
    return -ENOMEM;
Reason:
When kstrndup fails, the function returns -ENOMEM without executing the 'out' cleanup path (erofs_put_metabuf), causing a folio reference leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!sbi->volume_name) {
    ret = -ENOMEM;
    goto out;
}
Reason:
By setting ret to -ENOMEM and jumping to the 'out' label, the function ensures that erofs_put_metabuf is called to release the folio, fixing the reference leak.

